{"id": "EUVD-2026-105083", "enisaUuid": "f10cbce3-d824-332f-8ea0-2c6bf2ab1277", "description": "Stirling-PDF from 2.13.2 through 3.2.0 contains an incomplete denylist in DatabaseService.validateSqlContent() that allows administrators to bypass H2 import restrictions using CREATE OR REPLACE ALIAS. Authenticated administrators can upload a crafted SQL backup to the import-database endpoint, where RUNSCRIPT defines H2 Java function aliases and restores Java-method execution.", "datePublished": "2026-10-20T15:40:32", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-20T18:06:57", "baseScore": 8.6, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:H/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/abraxas/stirling-h2-import-leftover", "https://abraxaslabs.tech/research/stirling-h2-import-leftover", "https://abraxaslabs.tech/research/stirling-pdf-3.2.0-leftovers", "https://github.com/Stirling-Tools/Stirling-PDF/blob/v3.2.0/app/proprietary/src/main/java/stirling/software/proprietary/security/service/DatabaseService.java", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/stirling-pdf-2.13.2-through-3.2.0-h2-sql-denylist-bypass-via-import-database"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-113605", "GHSA-j8f5-2f4f-jm2m"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.66, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "6f1d2c13-50f4-38c5-9264-a53c94e8c272", "product": {"name": "Stirling-PDF", "vendor": {"name": "Stirling-Tools"}}, "product_version": "2.13.2 \u22643.2.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "eecf4370-1b3d-32dd-8f1c-ec61eff66806", "vendor": {"name": "Stirling-Tools"}}], "isExploited": false}